new-page: true 

= Kurt Pendrigon

Pendrigon works as a lawyer in Axton who defends left-wing individuals and causes. He favors cooperation with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> and a path of class struggle for the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>.

- @building_the_left
- @kpd_cooperation
- @prussian_bulwark
- @against_toleration
- @snap_election
- @root: Return to main

@building_the_left
title: Building the Left
subtitle: Push the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> to the left.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before next advisor action. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; left_strength += 6; left_dissent -= 8; reformist_dissent += 2

We have increased the strength of the left faction with the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>.

@kpd_cooperation
title: Cooperation with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>
subtitle: Push the party to be more friendly towards the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before next advisor action. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; left_strength += 5; collectivist_relation += 4*(1-dissent); reformist_dissent += 2; communist_coalition += 1 if collectivist_cooperation_seen <= 1; collectivist_cooperation_seen += 1

Through his work, Pendrigon has defended individual <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> members; this should make some connections possible.

@prussian_bulwark
title: The Heartland Bulwark
subtitle: As the Minister-President of Heartland, Pendrigon has power over the Heartland bureaucracy and security services.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0 and heartland_leader = "Pendrigon"
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before next advisor action. ?][? if heartland_leader != "Pendrigon" : Pendrigon doesn't control Heartland. ?]
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; heartland_affairs_timer -= 6; last_advisor_action = 1
go-to: prussian_affairs_left

@against_toleration
title: Against toleration
view-if: not constructive_vonc
subtitle: Break our current toleration arrangement, and bring down the government via a no-confidence vote.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before next advisor action. ?] [? if marcher_toleration == 0 : The <span style="color: #c00000;">Marchers</span> is not currently in toleration. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer == 0 and marcher_toleration
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; next_election_time = time + 3 if next_election_time > time+3; next_election_month = month + 3 if next_election_time >= time + 3; next_election_year = year if next_election_time >= time + 3; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; left_strength += 8; pro_republic -= 4; burgher_marcher -= 3; landed_marcher -= 3; guild_marcher -= 3; faithful_marcher -= 3; reformist_dissent += 8; left_dissent -= 5; gold_relation -= 4; unionist_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 4; ddp_right += 1; gold_right += 2; marcher_break_toleration += 1
go-to: new_prussia_election if in_social_catholic_coalition_heartland or in_weimar_coalition_heartland or in_grand_coalition_heartland or in_popular_front_heartland and ((center_right_coalition_heartland < 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate") or traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"); center_right_coalition_prussia if in_social_catholic_coalition_heartland or in_weimar_coalition_heartland or in_grand_coalition_heartland or in_popular_front_heartland and center_right_coalition_heartland >= 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"

We have grown tired of the burdens of toleration, and have called a vote of no confidence in the current minority government.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@new_prussia_election
on-arrival: unionist_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 4; collectivist_relation += 5; gold_right += 3; ddp_right += 2; lvp_right += 2; pro_republic -= 3; burgher_marcher -= 2; landed_marcher -= 2; guild_marcher -= 2; faithful_marcher -= 2; burgher_royalist += 2; guild_royalist += 2; landed_royalist += 2; faithful_royalist += 2; in_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_social_catholic_coalition_heartland = 0; in_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; in_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_popular_front_heartland = 0; in_left_front_heartland = 0; in_marcher_majority_heartland = 0; in_center_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_far_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; marcher_heartland = 0; right_heartland = 0; ddp_in_popular_front_heartland = 0; collectivist_goals_seen_heartland = 0; marcher_toleration_heartland = 0; heartland_coalition_trigger = 0
call: set_next_election_time_prussia

The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] has called a retaliatory vote in Heartland, forcing the dissolution of the state Assembly for new elections.

New Heartland elections have been set for [+ next_election_month_heartland : month +] [+ next_election_year_heartland +].

A double dissolution has shaken the people's faith in democracy, with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> exploiting the instability to claim that democracy is unworkable, and that the Commonwealth needs a strong leader.

@center_right_coalition_prussia
on-arrival: in_center_right_coalition_heartland = 1; in_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; in_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_popular_front_heartland = 0; in_left_front_heartland = 0; in_marcher_majority_heartland = 0; in_far_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; marcher_heartland = 0; right_heartland = 0; ddp_in_popular_front_heartland = 0; collectivist_goals_seen_heartland = 0; marcher_toleration_heartland = 0; heartland_coalition_trigger = 0; heartland_leader = "Sedgewick"; heartland_leader = "Askew" if unionist_leader == "Sedgewick"; burgher_marcher -= 3; unionist_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 4; gold_right += 3; ddp_right += 2; pro_republic -= 3; heartland_police_loyalty -= 0.06; heartland_police_strength -= 8; 

The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] has called a retaliatory no confidence vote in Heartland, replacing our government with a center-right coalition composed of all parties to our right, except for the <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span> and <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>. While this is a setback, it is not the worst possible outcome, as new elections could have led to significant gains for extremist parties.

[? if unionist_leader != "Sedgewick": Adam Sedgewick?][? if unionist_leader == "Sedgewick": Heinrich Askew?] of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is selected to be the Minister-President of Heartland.

@snap_election
title: Snap Election
subtitle: Call a snap election.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if chancellor != "Pendrigon" and president != "Pendrigon" : Pendrigon must be Chancellor or President. ?][? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before next advisor action. ?] [? if president = "Pendrigon" and presidential_powers : We have removed this power from the president with a constitutional reform. ?]
choose-if: advisor_action_timer == 0 and (chancellor == "Pendrigon" or (president == "Pendrigon" and not presidential_powers))
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; next_election_time = time + 3 if next_election_time > time+3; next_election_month = month + 3 if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year = year if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12; 

We have called for new elections, set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].